{"title":"2004 AIME II Problems/Problem 5","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><div id=\"toc\" class=\"toc\" role=\"navigation\" aria-labelledby=\"mw-toc-heading\"><input type=\"checkbox\" role=\"button\" id=\"toctogglecheckbox\" class=\"toctogglecheckbox\" style=\"display:none\" /><div class=\"toctitle\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2 id=\"mw-toc-heading\">Contents</h2><span class=\"toctogglespan\"><label class=\"toctogglelabel\" for=\"toctogglecheckbox\"></label></span></div>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-1\"><a href=\"#Problem\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-2\"><a href=\"#Solution_1\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 1</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-3\"><a href=\"#Solution_2\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">3</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 2</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-4\"><a href=\"#Solution_3_(Very_fast,_the_one_I_used_on_the_test)\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">4</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 3 (Very fast, the one I used on the test)</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-5\"><a href=\"#See_also\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">5</span> <span class=\"toctext\">See also</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2004_AIME_II_Problems/Problem_5&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>In order to complete a large job, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/e/e/6ee927e1332358c96c62c277441c907c4f51057f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1000$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"38\" height=\"14\" /> workers were hired, just enough to complete the job on schedule. All the workers stayed on the job while the first quarter of the work was done, so the first quarter of the work was completed on schedule. Then <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/5/9/e59e2c6e83eb78cca610a5fd4070ae01c8d4ae60.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$100$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"29\" height=\"14\" /> workers were laid off, so the second quarter of the work was completed behind schedule. Then an additional <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/5/9/e59e2c6e83eb78cca610a5fd4070ae01c8d4ae60.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$100$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"29\" height=\"14\" /> workers were laid off, so the third quarter of the work was completed still further behind schedule. Given that all workers work at the same rate, what is the minimum number of additional workers, beyond the <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/5/7/557a9700315ffdc6da28316197f148da6ee2a3ab.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$800$\" width=\"26\" height=\"12\" /> workers still on the job at the end of the third quarter, that must be hired after three-quarters of the work has been completed so that the entire project can be completed on schedule or before?\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_1\">Solution 1</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2004_AIME_II_Problems/Problem_5&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 1\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>A train is traveling at <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/e/e/6ee927e1332358c96c62c277441c907c4f51057f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1000$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"38\" height=\"14\" /> miles per hour and has one hour to reach its destination <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/e/e/6ee927e1332358c96c62c277441c907c4f51057f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1000$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"38\" height=\"14\" /> miles away. After <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/1/9/f1965fae079a9ba2c0726c307070c2355dfcb213.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$15$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" /> minutes and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/4/8/448b3c8f2596d1b93b4b3ef199f8b3241ced9da2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$250$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"29\" height=\"14\" /> miles it slows to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/d/d/fdd4beaeec1aa15c400a0763d78937b0385924b1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$900$\" width=\"26\" height=\"12\" /> mph, and thus takes <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/9/0/590f2347f5b50b8a52823b1a04e4404ce032a996.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{250}{900}(60)=\\frac{50}{3}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"108\" height=\"37\" /> minutes to travel the next <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/4/8/448b3c8f2596d1b93b4b3ef199f8b3241ced9da2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$250$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"29\" height=\"14\" /> miles. Then it slows to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/5/7/557a9700315ffdc6da28316197f148da6ee2a3ab.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$800$\" width=\"26\" height=\"12\" /> mph, so the next quarter takes <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/1/1/311ce1b1b514004b8b87099305decff9ce782dc4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{250}{800}(60)=\\frac{150}{8}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"117\" height=\"37\" />. The train then has <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/9/1/991f385013c19e24c2e935afa009e23d19142085.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$60-15-\\frac{50}{3}-\\frac{150}{8}=230/24$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"234\" height=\"37\" /> minutes left to travel 250 miles, and doing the arithmetic shows that during this last stretch it must travel more than <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/c/8/2c8f2ec4d050c27621a401a761e76835acb9c9c0.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1565$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"35\" height=\"13\" /> mph to make it on time. Therefore the company needs to add <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/8/e/a8e2951fbc55c0f39080ef9e56421569f507640f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1566-800 = \\boxed{766}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -6px\" width=\"150\" height=\"25\" /> more workers.\n</p><p>Solution by rocketscience\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_2\">Solution 2</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2004_AIME_II_Problems/Problem_5&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 2\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Let each worker's speed be <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/e/e/9ee4b825a2e36ae093ed7be5e4851ef453b34914.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$w$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"15\" height=\"10\" />, the entire time be <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/0/d/e0d2bf360290fd61d1c1557e763f2622363b3d35.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$t$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"8\" height=\"13\" />, and the total work be <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/c/e/dce34f4dfb2406144304ad0d6106c5382ddd1446.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />.\n</p><p><br />\nFrom the initial problem statement, we have <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/b/1/fb190d7b075995494c95d626973dab92dbbc1b0c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1000w\\cdot\\frac{1}{4}t=\\frac{1}{4}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"118\" height=\"37\" />.\n</p><p><br />\nWe need to find the time the next quarter takes to complete the same amount of work, which is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/6/9/b69da7db01dbe7dcfcfd2dc24502cdb342c56eb8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{1000}{900}\\cdot\\frac{1}{4}\\cdot t=\\frac{5}{18}t$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"138\" height=\"38\" />.\n</p><p><br />\nSimilarly, we find that the time the third quarter takes is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/c/a/3caabc0549624de6508cd9dd595573f57b17fda7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{1000}{800}\\cdot\\frac{1}{4}\\cdot t=\\frac{5}{16}t$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"138\" height=\"38\" />.\n</p><p><br />\nFinally, the time the last quarter takes is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/6/8/768289710fab81d0f2b3d2587f1e996b5173770c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$t\\left[1-\\left(\\frac{1}{4}+\\frac{5}{18}+\\frac{5}{16}\\right)\\right]=\\frac{23}{144}t$\" style=\"vertical-align: -17px\" width=\"249\" height=\"43\" />.\n</p><p><br />\nWe then let the number of workers needed be <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/e/26eeb5258ca5099acf8fe96b2a1049c48c89a5e6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"10\" />, so we have the equation <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/a/1/aa13bb600cfbc83f8c1dac5dc9693f367b4609f1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\left(800+x\\right)w\\cdot\\frac{23}{144}t=\\frac{1}{4}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"181\" height=\"38\" />. Dividing by the first equation, we have\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/b/f/1bff8a23feb2b142a371e63411cb69986b169f70.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\frac{800+x}{1000}\\cdot\\frac{\\frac{23}{144}}{\\frac{1}{4}}=1\\]\" width=\"135\" height=\"47\" />\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/6/0/66069ed545e1ae623d583c7d3e36614b8a478485.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\frac{800+x}{1000}\\cdot\\frac{23}{36}=1\\]\" width=\"129\" height=\"38\" />\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/7/6/276f38d24c3b8cf78474d4861a483b8b821771a3.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[800+x=\\frac{36000}{23}\\]\" width=\"131\" height=\"37\" />\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/a/9/ea982b5208db8e602f0393dde92bafa2cf929d74.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[x=\\frac{17600}{23}.\\]\" width=\"87\" height=\"37\" />\n</p><p>We can't have a part of a worker, so we take the ceiling of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/e/26eeb5258ca5099acf8fe96b2a1049c48c89a5e6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"10\" />, which we find to be <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/6/1/a610e07e3453565f930231ec6d97f4f969224343.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{766}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -6px\" width=\"40\" height=\"25\" />.\n</p><p>-flyhawkeye\n</p>\n<h2><span id=\"Solution_3_.28Very_fast.2C_the_one_I_used_on_the_test.29\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_3_(Very_fast,_the_one_I_used_on_the_test)\">Solution 3 (Very fast, the one I used on the test)</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2004_AIME_II_Problems/Problem_5&amp;action=edit&amp;section=4\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 3 (Very fast, the one I used on the test)\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Suppose <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/e/e/6ee927e1332358c96c62c277441c907c4f51057f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1000$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"38\" height=\"14\" /> workers can complete one quarter of the job in one day. After the first day, there were <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/d/d/fdd4beaeec1aa15c400a0763d78937b0385924b1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$900$\" width=\"26\" height=\"12\" /> workers remaining so the second quarter was completed in <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/7/1/6717255cb76cb21041a9c983b8ebd7b8fe68728b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{10}{9}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"20\" height=\"37\" /> days. Now there are only <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/5/7/557a9700315ffdc6da28316197f148da6ee2a3ab.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$800$\" width=\"26\" height=\"12\" /> workers remaining so the third quarter can be completed in <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/d/c/9dc8b6e819a6fa6b9fb99d47d1d48b892acb0aa1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{10}{8}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"20\" height=\"37\" /> days. It has been <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/5/4/154437832c74ec2d1f482456b3e0d7cf412c0ddb.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1+\\frac{10}{9}+\\frac{10}{8}=\\frac{121}{36}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"151\" height=\"37\" /> days since the job started, and we still have <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/5/e/f5ecb2e0a1fd26e92a970b3a046689f5a39e773e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{23}{36}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"20\" height=\"37\" /> days to complete the last quarter of the job, so we need <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/b/3/4b3f22278077266d8231a678f984ecb3ab186df1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{36}{23}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"20\" height=\"37\" /> of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/e/e/6ee927e1332358c96c62c277441c907c4f51057f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1000$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"38\" height=\"14\" /> workers, or <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/c/e/fce6c6614f32a3971b5645e763bd8d336f72e419.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1565.2173913$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"104\" height=\"13\" />. Since we can’t hire fractional workers, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/2/5/425365528dceffec8ffa37d1827bc4a4a6209703.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1566-800=\\boxed{766}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"149\" height=\"23\" /> must be the answer.\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"See_also\">See also</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2004_AIME_II_Problems/Problem_5&amp;action=edit&amp;section=5\" title=\"Edit section: See also\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black; width:80%;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2004_AIME_II\" title=\"2004 AIME II\">2004 AIME II</a></b> (<b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2004_AIME_II_Problems\" title=\"2004 AIME II Problems\">Problems</a></b> • <b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2004_AIME_II_Answer_Key\" title=\"2004 AIME II Answer Key\">Answer Key</a></b> • <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"http://www.artofproblemsolving.com/Forum/resources.php?c=182&amp;cid=45&amp;year=2004\">Resources</a>)\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Preceded&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2004_AIME_II_Problems/Problem_4\" title=\"2004 AIME II Problems/Problem 4\">Problem 4</a></b>\n</td>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Followed&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2004_AIME_II_Problems/Problem_6\" title=\"2004 AIME II Problems/Problem 6\">Problem 6</a></b>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td colspan=\"3\" style=\"text-align:center;\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2004_AIME_II_Problems/Problem_1\" title=\"2004 AIME II Problems/Problem 1\">1</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2004_AIME_II_Problems/Problem_2\" title=\"2004 AIME II Problems/Problem 2\">2</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2004_AIME_II_Problems/Problem_3\" title=\"2004 AIME II Problems/Problem 3\">3</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2004_AIME_II_Problems/Problem_4\" title=\"2004 AIME II Problems/Problem 4\">4</a> <b>•</b> <a class=\"mw-selflink selflink\">5</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2004_AIME_II_Problems/Problem_6\" title=\"2004 AIME II Problems/Problem 6\">6</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2004_AIME_II_Problems/Problem_7\" title=\"2004 AIME II Problems/Problem 7\">7</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2004_AIME_II_Problems/Problem_8\" title=\"2004 AIME II Problems/Problem 8\">8</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2004_AIME_II_Problems/Problem_9\" title=\"2004 AIME II Problems/Problem 9\">9</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2004_AIME_II_Problems/Problem_10\" title=\"2004 AIME II Problems/Problem 10\">10</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2004_AIME_II_Problems/Problem_11\" title=\"2004 AIME II Problems/Problem 11\">11</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2004_AIME_II_Problems/Problem_12\" title=\"2004 AIME II Problems/Problem 12\">12</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2004_AIME_II_Problems/Problem_13\" title=\"2004 AIME II Problems/Problem 13\">13</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2004_AIME_II_Problems/Problem_14\" title=\"2004 AIME II Problems/Problem 14\">14</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2004_AIME_II_Problems/Problem_15\" title=\"2004 AIME II Problems/Problem 15\">15</a>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td align=\"center\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=AIME_Problems_and_Solutions\" title=\"AIME Problems and Solutions\"> All AIME Problems and Solutions</a></b>\n</td></tr></tbody></table>\n<div class=\"print\">\n<div style=\"display:flex;width:100%;justify-content:space-between;align-items:center\">\n<div>\n<p><span class=\"mw-default-size\" typeof=\"mw:File\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=File:AMC_Logo.png\" class=\"mw-file-description\"><img src=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/images/d/d1/AMC_Logo.png\" decoding=\"async\" width=\"97\" height=\"84\" class=\"mw-file-element\" /></a></span>\n</p>\n</div>\n<div style=\"flex-grow:1;text-align:right\">\n<p>These problems are copyrighted &#169; by the <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://www.maa.org\">Mathematical Association of America</a>. \n</p>\n</div>\n<div style=\"clear:both;\"></div>\n</div></div>\n<!-- \nNewPP limit report\nCached time: 20261017202746\nCache expiry: 86400\nReduced expiry: false\nComplications: [show‐toc]\nCPU time usage: 0.041 seconds\nReal time usage: 0.062 seconds\nPreprocessor visited node count: 291/1000000\nPost‐expand include size: 1806/2097152 bytes\nTemplate argument size: 128/2097152 bytes\nHighest expansion depth: 3/100\nExpensive parser function count: 0/100\nUnstrip recursion depth: 0/20\nUnstrip post‐expand size: 7675/5000000 bytes\n-->\n<!--\nTransclusion expansion time report (%,ms,calls,template)\n100.00%   15.926      1 -total\n 57.28%    9.122      1 Template:AIME_box\n 40.83%    6.503      1 Template:MAA_Notice\n-->\n\n<!-- Saved in parser cache with key wiki-wiki_:pcache:2700:|#|:idhash:canonical and timestamp 20261017202746 and revision id 134131. Rendering was triggered because: api-parse\n -->\n</div>"}